      "snippet": {
        "text": "ChatGPT can be focused on working under specific data sets, making it perform customized tasks and generate accurate and prompt human-like responses. An excellent review of the pros and cons of ChatGPT in different aspects of human life is described by Dwivedi et al. (Dwivedi et al., 2023). In the future, evolutionary models based on reinforcement learning (Uc-Cetina et al., 2023) may open a new window to diverse and advanced possibilities of currently existing language models meanwhile addressing their drawbacks. \n\nDue to the diverse applications of large language models, it has been identified as a prospective study area. People at almost all stages of education -primary, secondary, tertiary, professional, research, teaching, etc. -could utilize LLMs in their respective areas of interest (Kasneci et al., 2023). Since individuals vary in their needs, abilities, skills, and preferences, platforms such as LLMs could be a good choice since they provide personalized and prompt responses based on the queries of their users. LLMs can assist school students not only in the development of reading skills, writing skills, and communication skills but also in enhancing their reading and writing style (El Shazly, 2021;Lin & Mubarok, 2021). LLMs can provide them with syntactic and grammatical corrections, help them comprehend complex texts, summarize theories, provide them with simple explanations and real-life examples on complex science topics, etc. LLMs could be used to generate quizzes and science problems, which help the students understand and retain what they have studied, which would help increase their critical thinking and ability to think out-of-the-box (Dijkstra et al., 2022;Gabajiwala et al., 2022). LLMs can enhance research skills in college students, whether undergraduate or postgraduate, and improve problem-solving skills and critical thinking capabilities.",
