        "text": "This study explored the effects of simulation-based inquiry activity designed to increase fifth-grade students' ability to identify variables. Findings indicate that while students are asked to design comparative experiments to verify their hypotheses autonomously, all students benefit from the Thermodynamics Challenge unit. Furthermore, students with low prior knowledge were more successful. This study confirmed the feasibility and effectiveness of using WISE units to improve science learning in the Chinese context and in elementary schools. \n\nThe study can make a unique contribution to the field of teaching comparative experiment with simulation embedded inquiry activities in elementary schools, while other studies have focused on scientific knowledge understanding in middle schools and above. The results of this study can provide primary science teachers with new approaches to teaching experimental design, remind them of the value of simulations as curricular materials that help all learners make progress in experimentation.",
